fix(web): keep the Projects sidebar to real, unfinished projects

The Projects sidebar filled up with rows that are not projects and rows
that are finished, and offered no way to act on either.

A pin no longer promotes a thread into Projects. A project is a top-level
thread that owns workers, or a thread explicitly marked as a project; the
pin goes back to doing one job, ordering the list. The menu's subproject
item now covers both directions of that mark: "Show as subproject" for a
nested thread, "Show in Projects" for a standing orchestrator between
jobs, and nothing for a thread whose workers already make it a project.
Project roots leave the Threads list whatever their pin state, so a
project and its orchestrator stop occupying both lists.

Settling a project folds it into Quiet straight away instead of waiting
out the seven-day quiet window. Attention and live work still win: a
settled project whose workers need you stays in the list.

Project rows take the same right-click menu every other thread row has,
so pin order, settle, nest and archive are reachable without the CLI.
Rename is left out there, since the row has no inline title editor.

